# Use your own Debian 13 VM over SSH instead of the Lima VM:
#   cp external-vm.conf.example external-vm.conf   (gitignored), edit, then: make deps, make vm-up, make provision.
# Delete external-vm.conf to go back to the Lima VM. One key=value per line, no trailing comments.
# The VM needs: fresh Debian 13, 4 CPU, 8 GiB RAM, 40 GiB disk, python3, key-based SSH, and passwordless
# sudo for the user (or user=root). make vm-up checks all of it. Guide: docs/install.md (your own Debian 13 VM).
host=192.168.64.10
user=debian
port=22
# Optional: private key to use (default: your ssh agent / ~/.ssh keys)
# ssh_key=~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# Optional: where the VM keeps etcd snapshots (make backups-pull copies them to ./backups)
# backup_dir=/var/backups/etcd
# The VM is air-gapped (a firewall keeps it so). host (default): its downloads go through this machine over SSH, to the
#   allowlisted sources in scripts/egress-allowlist.txt only. proxy: through your proxy, set below.
# egress=host
# proxy=http://10.0.0.5:3128   (an IP address: the VM has no DNS)
# Time sync: the firewall lets the VM reach these NTP servers (udp/123) only. Default: Google Public NTP (time.google.com).
# ntp=216.239.35.0,216.239.35.4
